{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והין צדק יהיה לכם", :translit "veh-ein tzedek yihyeh lakhem", :gloss "and a just hin shall you have"} {:he "ושמרתם את חקותי", :translit "ushmartem et chukotai", :gloss "and you shall keep My statutes"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut: adjacent verse placement links just measures to keeping all statutes"}], :frame {:text "The semikhut parshaniyya (contextual adjacency) he cites operates on Leviticus 19:36–19:37: the phrase 'and you shall keep My statutes' (Leviticus 19:37) directly follows the commandment of honest weights and measures (Leviticus 19:36), linking them. The broader principle that a single transgression can be reckoned as violating the entire corpus of commandments appears in several talmudic discussions (e.g., Shabbat 70a, Horayot 8a).", :sources ["Leviticus 19:36" "Leviticus 19:37" "Shabbat 70a" "Horayot 8a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "semikhut: adjacent verse placement links just measures to keeping all statutes", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:31.512400498Z", :model "glm-5.2"}